Add Snapshot Management for Safe Migration Rollback

Please enhance the Live Migration Operations module by adding a dedicated Snapshots feature alongside the existing Rollback functionality.

UI/UX Changes
Add a new Snapshots button immediately beside the Rollback button in the primary action toolbar.
The Snapshots feature should be easily accessible throughout the migration lifecycle and visually indicate whether snapshots are available for the selected migration or asset.
Purpose

Before any migration, remediation, or cryptographic upgrade is executed, QGuard Helix must automatically create a complete snapshot (backup) of the target asset's configuration and cryptographic state.

This ensures customers can safely restore their assets to their original pre-migration state if they:

Experience unexpected issues after migration.
Encounter compatibility problems with applications or services.
Need to revert during testing or validation.
Fail post-migration validation checks.
Decide to cancel or undo the migration.
Require recovery for business continuity or disaster recovery purposes.
